@hostAddress = https://localhost:7205
# With plain `dotnet run` (profile "http") only HTTP is served:
# @hostAddress = http://localhost:5053

### Import catalog (multipart/form-data)
# The multipart body needs an explicit boundary, and the file is attached with `< path`
# (relative to this .http file). `file=@path` is curl syntax and is not understood here.
POST {{hostAddress}}/api/catalog/imports
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----CatalogBoundary
Accept: application/json

------CatalogBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="ProductEntry.json"
Content-Type: application/json

< ../ProductEntry.json
------CatalogBoundary--

###
